<div class="callout"><div class="ct"><b>Backtest discipline honored, and its limits stated plainly:</b> every sweep here is segmented (fader-set vs full-set; per-regime leak buckets; per-day meter vs P&amp;L) — no blanket cross-tape number is offered as truth. But this is <b>one week, one summer range regime, in-sample, thin realised n, partly already gated</b>. The one deploy (action 1) is the only change both universes agree on across the whole grid; everything else is HOLD or TRIAL. The regime&rarr;exit R-target cheat-sheet (faders 0.5/1.5, momentum 1.5/2.5, trend 2.5/wide) remains an <b>unproven operator prior</b> — the exhaustion 0.5R/1.5R trial has fired exactly once, off-regime, so those Rs are NOT yet proven and should be swept per-regime once a trend week supplies the n. Re-run this whole review after the next real trend day before trusting any single-week dollar figure.</div></div>
